    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d866">

                <pb facs="1034" n="1024" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg1024"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50/2832b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to President Roosevelt
                    </hi><anchor n="14" xml:id="d866-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-20">October 20,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: Following our
                    conversation of October 13 [<hi rendition="#italic">12</hi>],<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d866-f2"/> I am sending you a memorandum on the scope of the United
                    Nations Relief and Rehabilitation Administration. The position taken in this
                    memorandum follows an exchange of views with Mr. Richard Law, in which Governor
                    Lehman participated, and I believe it represents the consensus of thinking on
                    this subject.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d866-f3"/> If it meets with your approval,
                    we will proceed accordingly to draft for your consideration instructions to Mr.
                    Dean Acheson, whom you have designated as the U.S. representative to
                        UNRRA.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d866-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>I am enclosing also a memorandum on finance, the result of discussions between
                    the Department of State and the Treasury Department. I gave you the gist of this
                    on Tuesday.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d866-f5"/> If it meets with your general
                    approval, I shall have appropriate legislation, together with a message to
                    Congress, drafted for your consideration.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d866-f6"/>
                </p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. R. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius, Jr</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>




                <xi:include href="d866-a1.xml" xpointer="d866-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d866-a2.xml" xpointer="d866-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d866-f1" n="14" type="source" xml:id="d866-f1-content">
                <p>The following marginal notation appears on copy of this letter which was returned
                    to Mr. Stettinius on October 26. “E.R.S. Jr. OK FDR.” (840.50/3252)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d866-f2" n="15" xml:id="d866-f2-content">
                <p>Mr. Stettinius’ conference with President Roosevelt was summarized in a
                    memorandum of telephone conversation by the Under Secretary of State with Judge
                    Rosenman on October 12; not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d866-f3" n="16" xml:id="d866-f3-content">
                <p>For text of resolution No. 1, Relating to the Scope of the Activities of the
                    Administration, adopted by the First Session of the Council, see Department of
                    State publication No. 2040, <hi rendition="#italic">First Session of the
                        Council</hi> …, p. 27.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d866-f4" n="17" xml:id="d866-f4-content">
                <p>Memorandum of October 12 regarding Mr. Acheson’s appointment, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d866-f5" n="18" xml:id="d866-f5-content">
                <p>October 19.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d866-f6" n="19" xml:id="d866-f6-content">
                <p>For messages to Congress by President Roosevelt and the Secretary of State
                    concerning proposed legislation on U.S. participation in UNRRA, see Department
                    of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, November 20, p. 372, and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., December 11, p. 416. For text of resolution
                    No. 14, Relating to a Financial Plan for the Administration, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">First Session of the Council</hi> …, p. 44.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
